  "summary": "Columbia (MO) Police Department released its 2025 Annual Surveillance Technology Report showing Flock Safety cameras generated 5,521 alerts in their first year, leading to 69 arrests among 217 case outcomes. The report details costs ($584,850 in year one), a 30-day data retention policy, sharing limited to Missouri law enforcement, and no substantiated complaints; the contract expires March 2027.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The Police Department received 5,521 total alerts from the Flock Safety system in 2025",
      "paragraph_idx": 2
    },
    {
      "quote": "Flock Safety collects vehicle data only, with no facial recognition, with data being purged every 30 days. Data is kept within the Columbia Police Department and only shared with other law enforcement agencies within Missouri",
      "paragraph_idx": 3
    },
    {
      "quote": "Flock is a force multiplier, not a standalone solution. It does not prevent crime by itself, nor does it replace traditional investigations, community policing or officer judgment.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "Columbia's contract with Flock Safety expires March 2027 when the city will renegotiate terms.",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    }
  ],
